<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  THE SUB-SCREEN EDITORS. Every string the settings and server sub-pages show.
  24-tab-conformance.md A-18 to A-36, 00-rules.md 9.
  ============================================================================

  These screens used to speak in four registers at once: upstream English left in
  values/, Russian hard-coded in Kotlin, «**» glued onto a system app's name by
  String.format, and menu titles that never appear anywhere a finger can reach. One
  file, one register: Russian, sentence case, formal «вы», hyphen never a dash, no
  emoji, no final period on a label, a period only where a sentence ends.

  Naming: the prefix is the screen, so a row's copy is findable from the layout that
  shows it - perapp_, routing_ed_, subs_, asset_, log_, about_, upd_, backup_, srv_.
  The shared empty and retry grammar is `editor_*` and every screen reuses it rather
  than writing its own «Ничего не найдено».
-->
